#: backends/platform/libretro/src/libretro-os-utils.cpp:238
msgid "## Libretro playlists for ScummVM core\nPlaylists used in Libretro frontends (e.g. Retroarch) are plain text lists used to directly launch a game with a specific core from the user interface. Those lists are structured to pass to the core the path of a specific content file to be loaded (e.g. ROM).\n\nScummVM core can accept as content the playlist-provided path to any of the files inside a valid game folder, the detection system will try to autodetect the game from the content file parent folder and run the game with default ScummVM options.\n\nThe core also supports dedicated per game **hook** plain text files with **."
msgstr "## 用於 ScummVM 核心的 Libretro 遊戲列表\nLibretro 前端（如 Retroarch）用到的遊戲列表是純文字列表，可用於呼叫使用者介面指定的核心來直接啟動遊戲。那些列表會向核心傳遞待載入的指定內容檔案（如 ROM）的路徑。\n\nScummVM 核心可接受有效遊戲資料夾內任何檔案的路徑作為內容，檢測系統將嘗試從內容檔案父資料夾自動檢測遊戲，並使用預設 ScummVM 選項執行遊戲。\n\n核心還支援使用“**”呼叫每個遊戲專用的**鉤子**純文字檔案。"

